# Blow AI — assistant rules (mirror of ARCHITECTURE.md)

Before creating or editing files, read `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and `backend/README.md`.

## Placement
- UI only in `frontend/`
- Agents in `backend/agents/` + wire `graph.py` / `state.py`
- Android/Appium in `backend/android*.py` and `backend/templates/`
- Safety/secrets in `backend/safety.py` (use `redact`)
- Tests in `tests/`; mark live/emulator work `@pytest.mark.slow`
- Docs in `docs/` or `project-docs/`; demo contracts in `demo-apps/`

## Constraints
- Prefer new modules &lt; 400 lines (&lt; 250 for new JS). Do not casually split existing 2k+ agent files without a full-suite PR.
- Separate UI from business logic; frontend must not invent verdicts.
- No hardcoded secrets; use `.env` / `BLOWAI_SECRET_*`; never commit `.env`.
- Reuse existing utilities before adding new ones.
- Do not add AI authorship watermarks or `Co-authored-by` AI tags.
- Never weaken irreversible-action blocks or write-guards.

## When you change the product
- New env var → update `.env.example` and README Configure section.
- New dependency → update `requirements.txt` / `constraints.txt` and run offline tests.
- Run `ruff check` and targeted offline pytest before done.
